// hunter.lang -- the rb labs prime gap hunter, written in Praetor.
//
//   hunter hunt P d m0 M SL L lambda mcal records.txt     the engine (same contract as the C hunt)
//   hunter bench [P d count]                              cpu vs gpu prime-test throughput
//   hunter serve [port]                                   the control room
//
// Praetor has no floating point, so the whole probability model is exact fixed-point integer
// arithmetic: probabilities are Q62 (1.0 = 2^62), logarithms are Q32, and every product goes
// through a 64x64 -> 128-bit multiply built from 32-bit halves. Big integers are GMP via FFI.

